cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pkd-alphagenome: a functional benchmark of AlphaGenome and SpliceAI at PKD1 and PKD2"
message: >-
  If you use this archive, cite both this record and the paper it supports.
  Licensing differs between the code, the model outputs and the third-party
  scores; see LICENSE and LEGALLY_BINDING_TERMS_OF_USE.txt before reuse.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Lawrence
    given-names: Christopher
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8159-0879"
abstract: >-
  A curated truth set of 125 PKD1 and PKD2 variants tested experimentally in 25
  published studies, each carrying a verbatim quotation from its source and a
  description validated against GRCh38, together with AlphaGenome, SpliceAI and
  CADD scores for those variants and for every single-nucleotide variant across
  both loci, the frozen analysis plan with its dated amendments, and the code
  that regenerates every reported number.
keywords:
  - autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease
  - PKD1
  - PKD2
  - RNA splicing
  - variant interpretation
  - AlphaGenome
  - SpliceAI
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23103370"
version: v1.0-jmg
repository-code: "https://github.com/PatientThread/pkd-alphagenome"
license-url: "https://github.com/PatientThread/pkd-alphagenome/blob/main/LICENSE"
